    "title": "New Moon of April 2026 | TheSkyLive",
    "text": "EnglishItalianoEspañol Home » Major Bodies » The Moon » Moon Calendar » 2026 » April » New Moon The new moon of April 2026 will occur on Friday, April 17 at 12:52 (Europe/London), with the Moon in the constellation Pisces, at a distance of 364,189 kilometers (226,297 miles) from Earth.This table summarizes the key facts of the new Moon of April 2026:DateFri Apr 17Time12:52TimezoneEurope/LondonDistance (km)364,189Distance (mi)226,297Diameter32.80'Magnitude-4.64RA (Apparent)01h 36m 28sDec (Apparent)+13° 18’ 21”RA (J2000)01h 35m 04sDec (J2000)+13° 10’ 19”ConstellationPisces Other Lunar Phases of April 2026 Full Moon of April 2026 Waxing Moon of April 2026 Waning Moon of April 2026 Lunar phase calendar of April 2026 Complete lunar calendar of the year 2026 Previous and Next Month New Moon of March 2026 New Moon of May 2026 Additional Resources on TheSkyLive The Moon: Complete reference information on TheSkyLive.com. Today's Moon Phase: Current phase of the Moon, high-resolution image of its present appearance and list of visible features. Next Full Moon: Precise date, time and visibility information of the next Full Moon. Next New Moon: Precise date, time and additional information about the next New Moon. Moon Calendar: Track the phases of the moon for each day. Lunar Eclipses: Extensive information about future and past lunar eclipses. Where is the Moon?: Key information on where to find the Moon in the sky. Distance of the Moon from Earth: Find out how far the Moon is from Earth right now. How Bright is the Moon?: Current visual brightness (magnitude) and apparent size. Rise and Set Times: Rise and set times of the Moon from your location. Interactive Sky Map: Planetarium-style interactive visualization of the Moon's position in the sky. Ephemeris: 15 days the Moon's computed ephemeris.",
